 "section_summary": "This section primarily comprises Foreign Service Despatch No. 581 (September 4, 1948) from the U.S. Political Adviser for Japan in Tokyo transmitting a comprehensive 48-page statistical survey compiled by the SCAP Economic and Scientific Section's Labor Division on Japanese labor unions and federations as of December 31, 1947. The survey provides exhaustive data across twenty-five tables detailing union membership, national federation affiliations (including Sodomei and Sanbetsu), industrial distribution, collective bargaining agreements, dues collection methods, union-management councils, and prefectural breakdowns. Additionally, the section includes an unrelated inquiry letter dated April 16, 1948, from a resident of Glyfada, Greece, requesting information from the State Department regarding the wartime disappearance of the Nichiran Aluminium Company Ltd. in Tokyo and persons connected with it.",
