   "summary": "Compiled by SCAP's Labor Division from Japanese Ministry of Labor data, this report analyzes 28,053 local unions comprising 6,371,188 members (37 percent of the industrial labor force) as of December 31, 1947. Twenty-five statistical tables provide comprehensive breakdowns by industry, sex, prefecture, founding date, dues collection methods, paid union officials, and local union-management councils. The report also details union affiliations across major national federations, independent national unions, government workers' bodies, and unaffiliated organizations, alongside data on collective bargaining agreements.",
